Checkpoint 13 four-day full live test
=====================================

Purpose and boundaries
----------------------

This run exercises all registered streams for Windy, Fintraffic, and Skaping
for four days. Initial polling is deterministically staggered over ten minutes.
The three workers run independently and restart only after unexpected failure.
This observation does not deliberately inject failures or perform restart,
restore, or recovery drills.

Database pools are limited to 60 connections for Windy, 20 for Fintraffic,
and 8 for Skaping. The combined ceiling of 88 leaves PostgreSQL headroom for
monitoring, discovery, maintenance, and administrative access.

Discovery is live (not dry-run), sequentially ordered Windy, Fintraffic, then
Skaping, and scheduled daily at 12:00 UTC. S3 cleanup runs daily at 00:15 UTC
and removes canonical image objects older than 24 hours. A database backup
runs daily at 01:00 UTC. The target stops its workers and timers automatically
four days after it starts; monitoring infrastructure is deliberately left
running so the final dashboards remain available.

Provider freshness and image-download retries are explicitly zero for this
test. The validated request pacing is 0.01 seconds for Windy and 0.1 seconds
for Fintraffic and Skaping. S3 upload and MQTT publication retain their
configuration from `.env` (both default to one retry).

One-time installation from the administrator account
-----------------------------------------------------

    sudo bash -c \
      'cp /home/codexuser/src/webcam-iot-ingest/deployment/systemd/checkpoint13-four-day-live-test/webcam-checkpoint13-* /etc/systemd/system/'
    sudo systemctl daemon-reload
    sudo systemd-analyze verify \
      /etc/systemd/system/webcam-checkpoint13-*.service \
      /etc/systemd/system/webcam-checkpoint13-*.timer \
      /etc/systemd/system/webcam-checkpoint13-*.target

The administrator should install the narrow sudo policy shown after this
runbook. Do not grant unrestricted `systemctl` or general root access.

Preflight from the codexuser account
------------------------------------

    cd /home/codexuser/src/webcam-iot-ingest
    git status --short --branch
    docker compose --env-file .env --profile monitoring config --quiet
    systemd-analyze verify \
      deployment/systemd/checkpoint13-four-day-live-test/*.service \
      deployment/systemd/checkpoint13-four-day-live-test/*.timer \
      deployment/systemd/checkpoint13-four-day-live-test/*.target
    grep -E '^(S3_UPLOAD|MQTT_PUBLICATION)_RETRY_COUNT=' .env || true

Start and inspect from the codexuser account
--------------------------------------------

    sudo -n systemctl start webcam-checkpoint13-four-day.target
    sudo -n systemctl --no-pager --full status \
      webcam-checkpoint13-four-day.target \
      webcam-checkpoint13-ingestion@windy.service \
      webcam-checkpoint13-ingestion@fintraffic.service \
      webcam-checkpoint13-ingestion@skaping.service
    sudo -n systemctl list-timers --all --no-pager \
      'webcam-checkpoint13-*'

The worker commands must contain no country restriction and no five-job
checkpoint-12 bound. Confirm their metrics on ports 8013, 8014, and 8015:

    for port in 8013 8014 8015; do
      echo "Port $port"
      curl -fsS "http://127.0.0.1:${port}/metrics" |
        grep -E '^webcam_(ingestion_epoch_total|source_stream_due_count)'
    done

Follow operation and dashboards
-------------------------------

    sudo -n journalctl -f \
      -u 'webcam-checkpoint13-ingestion@*.service' \
      -u webcam-checkpoint13-discovery-sequence.service \
      -u webcam-checkpoint13-spool-cleanup.service \
      -u webcam-checkpoint13-db-backup.service

Use the existing local tunnel to Grafana on port 3000. Review all three worker
and discovery dashboards, Maintenance jobs, and Infrastructure health.

Stop early or confirm the automatic stop
----------------------------------------

    sudo -n systemctl stop webcam-checkpoint13-four-day.target
    sudo -n systemctl --no-pager --full status \
      webcam-checkpoint13-four-day.target \
      webcam-checkpoint13-ingestion@windy.service \
      webcam-checkpoint13-ingestion@fintraffic.service \
      webcam-checkpoint13-ingestion@skaping.service
    sudo -n systemctl list-timers --all --no-pager \
      'webcam-checkpoint13-*'

Stopping the target stops the three workers and all four test timers. It does
not stop the Compose monitoring infrastructure.

Restricted sudo policy
----------------------

From the administrator account:

    sudo visudo -f /etc/sudoers.d/webcam-checkpoint13

Install the following policy (verify `/usr/bin/systemctl` and
`/usr/bin/journalctl` with `command -v` on the host if they differ):

    Cmnd_Alias WEBCAM_CP13 = \
        /usr/bin/systemctl start webcam-checkpoint13-four-day.target, \
        /usr/bin/systemctl stop webcam-checkpoint13-four-day.target, \
        /usr/bin/systemctl --no-pager --full status webcam-checkpoint13-*, \
        /usr/bin/systemctl list-timers --all --no-pager webcam-checkpoint13-*, \
        /usr/bin/journalctl -f -u webcam-checkpoint13-*

    codexuser ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: WEBCAM_CP13

Then:

    sudo chown root:root /etc/sudoers.d/webcam-checkpoint13
    sudo chmod 0440 /etc/sudoers.d/webcam-checkpoint13
    sudo visudo -c

The shell quotes around `webcam-checkpoint13-*` are not passed to sudo. If the
host's sudo command matching does not accept a requested multi-unit inspection,
inspect one unit at a time using the same command form.
